# NET-TELEPORT-ENCROACH: a server teleport lands the pawn on a valid spot (UE AActor::TeleportTo ->
# UWorld::FindTeleportSpot; AGameModeBase::RestartPlayer through the same placement). The simulation holds a pending
# placement per pawn (Net/MeshOfOne.hpp Pawn::Pending), asks the server's world whether the destination is resident
# (Net::IWorldResidency, ServerWorld::ResidencyAt) and the game where the capsule may stand (Net::IPawnPlacer,
# Gameplay::FindTeleportSpot: lifted out of the ground, snapped onto the floor, refused over nothing). A falling
# pawn never passes 4000 cm/s (Gameplay::kTerminalVelocityCmPerS).
# Before this feature (scn-1127-020957): `teleport 1 40000 300 3000` put the capsule 276 cm under the landscape
# (ground 576 cm) and the pawn fell for 116 s to y=-6.66e6 (server.log:1246); a teleport to (200000, 300, 3000), in
# no cell of the grid, was accepted. The console printed nothing but "player N has no pawn".
# Played by scripts/Dev/net_scenario.py. A's frames come from its pawn camera (--shot-player-view): the landing is what
# A sees. A sprints +X; its scripted walk ends at 300 m (server position), and the teleports come after it stopped, so
# no input moves the landed pawn and the residency union 5 s later must hold the very spot. B joins only then, so
# every pawn-1 velocity B ever receives is after the walk (a non-zero one is the slide of D4).
# Net coordinates are Y-up (X, Y, Z), cm.
Мир Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
